Analog Audio Conditioning & Passive Fader Mixer Schematic
​1. AD9850 Sine Bass (ZOUT1) Conditioning:
​Route ZOUT1 through a 4.7 µF to 10 µF DC-blocking capacitor (positive leg toward ZOUT1 if electrolytic) with a 47 kΩ resistor to GND.  
​For Analog Warmth / Growl, pass that AC-coupled signal through a 1 kΩ resistor into two anti-parallel diodes (1N4148 or 1N34A, one anode-to-GND and one cathode-to-GND), then through a passive RC low-pass filter (2.2 kΩ series resistor + 100 nF cap to GND, ~720 Hz cutoff).  

​2. Summing / Mixer Bus:
​Sum the conditioned AD9850 sine bass (via a 10 kΩ mixing resistor or fader) with the AD9850 square wave (QOUT1) and Si5351A CLK0 / CLK1 
outputs(each through a DC-blocking cap 
and 22 kΩ–47 kΩ resistor/fader).